Payload list: --ape-list prints every payload member, one per line, sorted, in the
spelling --ape-unpack takes, so a reader learns what a binary carries without unpacking
anything. It takes no argument and has no short form. It is settled ahead of the boot
like unpack, so no distribution ever sees the flag; a build without a payload says so
and fails.

